<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Fashion Weapon</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 1)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>fashion arrow
fashion quarter staff
fashion trap
fashion bow
fashion fighting staff
</pre>
<p>Carves a weapon from a fallen branch: arrows, a quarter staff, a trap, a 
bow or a fighting staff. You need the wood of a forest, so you can only do 
it in a forest, and it takes a little while and some endurance. What you 
can make grows with your skill:
</p>
<pre>arrows            from the start
quarter staff     from 25% skill
trap              from 50%
bow               from 75%
fighting staff    at 100%
</pre>
<p>The better your skill, the finer the work: a master's weapons are well 
crafted and even carry a little magic (see <a cmd='#'>Help Craftsmanship</a>). You can't 
fashion while fighting, or make two things at once.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Craftsmanship</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ranger Skills</a>
</pre>




</div>